.TH MAKEMKV-TUI 1 "@DATE@" "makemkv-tui @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
makemkv-tui \- keyboard-driven MakeMKV frontend
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B makemkv-tui
.RI [ options ] " [source]"
.br
.B makemkv-tui batch
.I INPUT
.B --output
.I OUTPUT
.br
.B makemkv-tui batch --resume
.I STATE
.RB [ --retry-failed ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Browse title and stream metadata and select titles for extraction with the
separately installed makemkvcon engine. Source track rows are read-only.
Batch mode plans all discovered ISOs before explicit extraction confirmation.
Completed titles are verified and tracked in persistent JSON for recovery.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the frontend version without starting the engine.
.TP
.B --help
Show command help. Use batch --help for batch options.
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Use the given frontend preferences file.
.TP
.BI --profile " PATH"
Use an existing MakeMKV profile; effects depend on the installed engine.
.TP
.BI "batch --state " PATH
Save a new plan at an explicit path.
.TP
.B batch --plans
Choose a saved batch in the terminal UI.
.TP
.B batch --list
List saved batches.
.TP
.B batch --state-dir
Print the default batch-state directory.
.SH KEYS
Up/Down navigate visible rows. Left/Right or Tab fold the tree.
Space toggles a title; A/D select/deselect all titles.
Enter/PgDn advances batch planning, PgUp goes back, X skips, F shows summary.
In the summary Enter opens confirmation; Y starts extraction.
Ctrl+C stops immediately; another Ctrl+C forces termination.
S finishes the current ISO then pauses. Ctrl+L opens logs; Ctrl+E expands errors.
.SH FILES
Default batch plans: $XDG_STATE_HOME/makemkv-tui/batches/ or
$HOME/.local/state/makemkv-tui/batches/.
Explicit legacy plan paths remain supported.
.SH NOTES
The frontend is MIT licensed. MakeMKV is not bundled and has separate license
and usage requirements. Preserve JSON and staging data when publication fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
The installed README.md and BATCH.md, and makemkv-tui batch --help.
